From 6cef517d47c3e60571c1ce85a4cc5d97d5663602 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: API Demo <api-demo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:37:25 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] API Demo: import DeepSeek chat history as real sessions

dsh-go-bridge gets GET|POST /dsh-go/v1/sessions/import (capability
session-import). The page parses the export and sends normalized
conversations in batches; each becomes a closed session log through the
public sessionPersistence seam, without patching DSH:

- completed turns, an empty system head at surface node 0 (the agent loop
  replaces it with the live prompt when the chat continues), a user title
  with no messageSeqs, and an ignorable plugin:dsh-go/import record;
- ids derived from (source, sourceId), so a second import skips, and the
  next generation once safe deletion has tombstoned an id;
- each log is read back (the read path validates what append does not)
  and folded into the projection cache, so the list shows titles at once.

runtime/tests/session-import.test.mjs covers the builder and route;
session-import-live.py runs a real DSH host with a fake model (stock and
dsh-Go-patched 0.2.2-rc.1 both pass).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
